    <!-- marinaMoji Preferences localisation top-up -->
    <message>
        <source>Input mode</source>
        <translation>Input mode</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Sets the default writing mode when marinaMoji starts: hiragana, katakana, half-width katakana, or direct (Latin) input. You can still change mode from the toolbar or keyboard while typing.</source>
        <translation>Sets the default writing mode when marinaMoji starts: hiragana, katakana, half-width katakana, or direct (Latin) input. You can still change mode from the toolbar or keyboard while typing.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Punctuation style</source>
        <translation>Punctuation style</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Chooses whether period and comma keys produce Japanese punctuation (、。) or Western forms (，．) while composing.</source>
        <translation>Chooses whether period and comma keys produce Japanese punctuation (、。) or Western forms (，．) while composing.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Japanese  、。
Alternative  ，．</source>
        <translation>Japanese  、。
Alternative  ，．</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Symbol style</source>
        <translation>Symbol style</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Controls whether symbols such as brackets and currency signs are inserted in fullwidth or halfwidth form by default.</source>
        <translation>Controls whether symbols such as brackets and currency signs are inserted in fullwidth or halfwidth form by default.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Space input style</source>
        <translation>Space input style</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Decides whether the space bar inserts a fullwidth or halfwidth space, or follows the current character-width rules.</source>
        <translation>Decides whether the space bar inserts a fullwidth or halfwidth space, or follows the current character-width rules.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Automatically switch to halfwidth</source>
        <translation>Automatically switch to halfwidth</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>After certain punctuation, marinaMoji can switch temporarily to halfwidth input so Latin letters and digits stay compact without leaving Japanese mode.</source>
        <translation>After certain punctuation, marinaMoji can switch temporarily to halfwidth input so Latin letters and digits stay compact without leaving Japanese mode.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Convert at punctuations</source>
        <translation>Convert at punctuations</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>When enabled, typing selected punctuation (。、? !) ends the current phrase and converts it automatically, similar to pressing Space then Enter on many Japanese IMEs. Use the checkboxes to choose which marks trigger conversion.</source>
        <translation>When enabled, typing selected punctuation (。、? !) ends the current phrase and converts it automatically, similar to pressing Space then Enter on many Japanese IMEs. Use the checkboxes to choose which marks trigger conversion.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Initial conversion mode</source>
        <translation>Initial conversion mode</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Manual mode waits for Space (or your convert key) before showing kanji candidates. Live mode offers conversions while you type, which feels closer to predictive input.</source>
        <translation>Manual mode waits for Space (or your convert key) before showing kanji candidates. Live mode offers conversions while you type, which feels closer to predictive input.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Two-step Enter after conversion</source>
        <translation>Two-step Enter after conversion</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>When enabled, the first Enter confirms the conversion candidate and the second Enter commits the text. Useful if you often refine candidates before inserting them. This option is experimental.</source>
        <translation>When enabled, the first Enter confirms the conversion candidate and the second Enter commits the text. Useful if you often refine candidates before inserting them. This option is experimental.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Initial kanji style</source>
        <translation>Initial kanji style</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Shin (modern) forms are everyday shinjitai. Kyū (traditional) converts dictionary results toward kyūjitai using OpenCC and marinaMoji’s custom tables—helpful for historical texts. You can still toggle shin/kyū from the toolbar while writing.</source>
        <translation>Shin (modern) forms are everyday shinjitai. Kyū (traditional) converts dictionary results toward kyūjitai using OpenCC and marinaMoji’s custom tables—helpful for historical texts. You can still toggle shin/kyū from the toolbar while writing.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Shin  国 学
Kyū   國 學</source>
        <translation>Shin  国 学
Kyū   國 學</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Detailed width rules</source>
        <translation>Detailed width rules</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>For each character group (letters, digits, punctuation, and so on), choose whether composition and conversion should prefer fullwidth or halfwidth forms. This table is the fine-grained companion to the simpler spacing and symbol settings above.</source>
        <translation>For each character group (letters, digits, punctuation, and so on), choose whether composition and conversion should prefer fullwidth or halfwidth forms. This table is the fine-grained companion to the simpler spacing and symbol settings above.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Learning / personalization</source>
        <translation>Learning / personalization</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Controls how strongly past conversions influence new suggestions. Clear personalization data removes that learned history; it does not delete your user dictionary entries.</source>
        <translation>Controls how strongly past conversions influence new suggestions. Clear personalization data removes that learned history; it does not delete your user dictionary entries.</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Personal dictionary</source>
        <translation>Personal dictionary</translation>
    </message>
    <message>
        <source>Your own readings and spellings—names, archaic forms, specialist terms. Edit user symbols maintains short strings that appear on the User tab of the toolbar Symbols palette.</source>
        <translation>Your own readings and spellings—names, archaic forms, specialist terms. Edit user symbols maintains short strings that appear on the User tab of the toolbar Symbols palette.</translation>
